cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Cite this repository as research software and an evaluation protocol. No GPU research results or paper publication are claimed."
type: software
title: "RSI-Audit: Budget-Constrained Auditing of Self-Improving Coding Agents"
version: "0.2.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/rita2126top-alt/rsi-audit-proposal"
url: "https://github.com/rita2126top-alt/rsi-audit-proposal"
authors:
  - name: "rita2126top-alt"
    website: "https://github.com/rita2126top-alt"
abstract: >-
  Proposed evaluation of reused validation panels, disjoint one-use panels,
  and a terminal validation gate for persistent coding-agent harness
  improvement with a frozen open model and independent final auditing.
  This version contains executable search, isolated execution and scoring,
  frozen independent auditing, paired analysis, tests, and verified references.
  CPU and synthetic pipeline validation are complete. Real Docker and GPU
  integration and formal experiments have not been executed.
keywords:
  - agent evaluation
  - self-improvement
  - adaptive validation
  - reproducibility
license: MIT
